{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "NMR", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (88.89%) to insect AalCecA GRAVY:-0.02; M Wt: 3676.509; Mol formula: C169H300N48O42; Mol ex coeff: 0. Activity: active against E. coli strains ATCC 25922, EcESBL1, Ec2, EcESBL3, EcNMD1, EcOXA48 (MIC 2-4 ug/ml), P. aeruginosa strains ATCC 17978, Pa1, Pa2, Pat3 (MIC 1-4 ug/ml), A. baumannii strains ATCC 17978, ab1, ab2, ab3 (MIC 1-2 ug/ml), K. pneumoniae KpKPC or KpVIM (MIC 1-2 ug/ml), S-aureus/MRSA (>32 ug/ml), E-faecalis and E-faecium. Activity is salt-insensitive. Structure: helical in SDS micelles based on both CD and NMR. Structure is depicted as helix-bend-helix.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "25162372", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "PLoS One. 2014 Aug 27;9(8):e105441. doi: 10.1371/journal.pone.0105441. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03507", "source_id": "AP03507", "source_numeric_id": "03507", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03507", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Aedesin: structure and antimicrobial activity against multidrug resistant bacterial strains.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
{"activity_text": "Antimicrobial, Antibacterial, Anti-Gram+, Anti-Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "The anti-bacterial activity of Aedesin was found to be salt-resistant, indicating that it is active under physiological conditions encountered in body fluids characterized by ionic salt concentrations.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "Not included yet", "hemolytic_activity_text": "No hemolysis information or data found in the reference(s) presented in this entry", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "17510324##25162372", "record_granularity": "source_table_row", "reference_text": "Science 316:1718-1723(2007).##PLoS ONE 9:e105441-e105441(2014).", "sequence_key": "DRAMP:DRAMP18194", "source_id": "DRAMP18194", "source_numeric_id": "", "source_path": "DRAMP/dramp_downloads_2026-04-02/raw/Anti-Gram-_amps.txt", "source_record_id": "Anti-Gram-_amps:DRAMP18194", "source_table": "Anti-Gram-_amps.txt", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "Gram-negative (including drug-resistent): E. coli (MIC 2-4 ug/mL), P. aeruginosa (MIC 1-4 ug/mL), A. baumannii (MIC 1-2 ug/mL), K. pneunomiae (MIC 1-2 ug/mL).##No antibacterial effects of the peptide were observed against different isolates of Gram-positive S. aureus, E. faecalis and E. faecium strains showing MIC values over 32. (Pubmed:25162372)", "title": "Genome sequence of Aedes aegypti, a major arbovirus vector.##Aedesin: structure and antimicrobial activity against multidrugresistant bacterial strains.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "DRAMP"}
